From: w8 <w8@local>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:17:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] collision.ATTRACT_CONTACT_MEAN =
 client16402_in_mean_uncapped: a contact mean that holds a pull is not capped
 at 150

Mechanic: under client15535_in_mean a pulled unit with a contact takes the pull as one entry of its contact accumulator, and
move16402 collision_mean then caps the whole mean at 150. A fast unit's pull (Speed 120 under a Tornado: 432 a tick) in a pack is
cut to 150 against its walk: the engine's Royal Hogs closed on the centre at ~30 a tick. New arm client16402_in_mean_uncapped
(shipped): the same mean, but one holding a pull is not cut (state.rs `cap_back` puts back what the cap takes). Old arms
after_mean and client15535_in_mean kept; CLIENT15535_ARMS keeps client15535_in_mean for 15.535.29 captures (their rows never
reached the cap). A knockback ladder or a death slide is untouched (still after the mean).

Minimal reproduction: tests/attract_mean_uncapped.rs: tests/attract_contact_mean.rs's scene with Hog Riders (a 432 pull, where
the Knight's 216 never meets the cap): from the first contact tick the uncapped step goes further toward the Tornado. Plant
attract_mean_capped turns it red.

Parity-Evidence: ClashBot scratchpad/gauntlet/L74/parity/fin15 (FIN15.md section 4; j2diag.py, law_ab.sh, analysis/torn_ab_*.txt):
- live, 9 Tornado casts on Royal Hogs (36 hogs, e.g. 20261017_040555 t1304-t1320): hogs in contact close on the centre at 80-150
  a tick, the capped engine at 25-65;
- A/B on the 638 captured client 16.402 frame logs (one wheel, K = 0, PARITY_OVERRIDES): J2 Tornado end point within 0.5 tile
  0.821 -> 0.880 (1,540 bodies), all spells 0.904 -> 0.914; mass 1 0.59 -> 0.75, mass 2 0.66 -> 0.81, mass 4 0.82 -> 0.88, no
  mass class lower; Royal Hogs 0.32 -> 0.72 (n 47), Hog Rider 0.81 -> 0.93 (54), Minion Horde 0.71 -> 0.82 (180), Goblin Gang
  0.76 -> 0.86 (51); J3 king wakes on a damage trigger after our Tornado 0.569 -> 0.641 (184); J6 0.692 -> 0.694.
Open: the Evo Royal Hogs stay at 0.41 (n 32); the exact 16.402 form (no cap vs a larger cap) is not separated.
